WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.650
SOC 2 reports are commonly discussed as Type I or Type II.

2
00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:07.903
The difference is about timing and what the auditors evaluate.

3
00:00:07.903 --> 00:00:13.770
A Type I report evaluates whether controls are suitably designed at a specific point in time.

4
00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:20.145
It answers whether the control design appears appropriate for the selected criteria and scope on a defined date.

5
00:00:20.145 --> 00:00:27.788
A Type II report evaluates whether controls are suitably designed and operated effectively over a defined review period.

6
00:00:27.788 --> 00:00:33.605
That period is often several months, depending on the engagement and customer expectations.

7
00:00:33.605 --> 00:00:41.288
Type I can be useful when an organization is starting its SOC 2 journey or wants an initial independent view of control design.

8
00:00:41.288 --> 00:00:45.399
It can show that the organization has put a control framework in place.

9
00:00:45.399 --> 00:00:53.411
Type II usually provides stronger operational assurance because it examines whether controls were performed over time.

10
00:00:53.411 --> 00:01:00.755
Customers often prefer Type II reports because they show sustained operation rather than only point-in-time design.

11
00:01:00.755 --> 00:01:04.606
Neither report type should be described as a badge that ends the work.

12
00:01:04.606 --> 00:01:11.281
Controls still need ownership, evidence, monitoring, maintenance, and improvement after the report is issued.

13
00:01:11.281 --> 00:01:14.125
Understanding the difference helps teams prepare.

14
00:01:14.125 --> 00:01:21.489
Type I emphasizes readiness on a date, while Type II emphasizes consistent operation during the audit period.

15
00:01:21.489 --> 00:01:26.318
For teams doing the work, Type II usually requires stronger habits.

16
00:01:26.318 --> 00:01:34.649
Controls need to happen repeatedly, exceptions need to be tracked, and evidence needs to show that the process was followed throughout the review window.
